{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>על</b> — The words of the prophet concern what the servants of HaShem would lament in those days." "<b>שולל</b> — Like a person whose garments were stripped off and he remains naked. Or he mentioned שולל because a madman, who is deranged in mind, his way is to go שולל and naked, and it is from the root שובב. So too the meaning of מוליך יועצים שולל." "<b>וערום</b> — Without clothing. And he is not called ערום when clothed in sackcloth, but only when he removes the sack, as he said in Isaiah: ופתחת השק מעל מתניך ונעלך תחלץ — ויעש כן הלך ערום ויחף."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:33.454434411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}